    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15374": {
      "title": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | Physics Program - Teaching Assistant (Physics Lab) (2026/2027)",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | Physics Program - Teaching Assistant (Physics Lab) (2026/2027) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Physics Program - Teaching Assistant (Physics Lab) (2026/2027) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title Physics Program - Teaching Assistant (Physics Lab) (2026/2027) Student Position Type Non Federal Work Study/La Verne Work Appointment Type Part-Time FTE Work Schedule TA will work one or two of the following lab sections: Tuesday 02:00 PM – 05:00 PM Tuesday 06:50 PM – 09:50 PM Wednesday 01:00 PM – 04:00 PM Wednesday 06:00 PM – 09:00 PM Thursday 02:00 PM – 05:00 PM Thursday 06:50 PM – 09:50 PM Mandatory Pre-Lab Meetings: Fridays (time to be decided) Attend mandatory weekly pre-lab meetings. Department Manager Hiring Manager Jignesh Patel Number of Vacancies 10 Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary Lab instructors will rely on their teaching assistants to provide valuable instructional/grading support and offer their unique insights for improving the labs from a student perspective. While helping fellow students learn physics, teaching assistants will become better teachers, better learners, better communicators, and improve their own understanding of physics. Specific Duties Teaching assistants will: Help students to safely and effectively use specialized scientific apparatuses, computerized data acquisition systems, and data analysis techniques. Facilitate small group interactions and deep discussions about theoretical and experimental physics phenomena. Assist instructors with conceptual introductions, troubleshooting equipment malfunctions, and grading as necessary. Attend mandatory weekly pre-lab meetings. Minimum Qualifications Must be current University of La Verne student. Successful completion of the Physics sequence 201/203 or 202/204 with a grade of B- or better. Interest in physical science Preferred Qualifications Committed to working both Fall and Spring semesters for a minimum of 5 hours/week. Ability to communicate effectively and help students construct their own understandings of lab material. Dependable, reliable, and self-sufficient. Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. Physical Demands Summary The physical demands include the ability to sit, stand, walk, bend, and lift up to 20 pounds occasionally. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? No If yes, list maximum weight and duration Describe work environment Physics Laboratory Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $16.90 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251532SE Special Instructions to Applicants Open Date 06/01/2025 Close Date 06/01/2027 Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15340 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is/was your major field of study? (Open Ended Question) Anticipated Graduation Date? (Open Ended Question) Cumulative GPA? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter Resume University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15697": {
      "title": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | Instructor, Psychology (NTT)",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | Instructor, Psychology (NTT) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Instructor, Psychology (NTT) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The University of La Verne is unable to provide sponsorship for work visas at this time. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for visa sponsorship now or in the future. Job Vacancy Position Information Functional Title Instructor, Psychology (NTT) Position Details University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary The University of La Verne’s College of Health and Community Well-Being invites applications for a full-time, ten-month, non-tenure-track Instructor position to begin with the 2026-2027 academic year. This year-to-year position will be responsible for supporting the successful implementation and operation of the University of La Verne’s Certified Wellness Coach Education Program funded through the Health Care Access and Information ( HCAI ) initiative. This position is housed within the undergraduate Psychology program and would focus on the development of the Wellness Coaching Minor and serve as internship coordinator for all undergraduate programs in Psychology. The annual appointment is initially a one-year appointment, renewable based on the evolving needs of Wellness Coach program and the College. Teaching 6 courses per year in the areas of Psychology, with a particular emphasis on courses in applied areas that relate to Social Work. Coordinate with qualifying placement sites, internship partners, clinical/community-based organizations, and employment agencies to facilitate student experiential learning opportunities. Establish and maintain partnerships that support student workforce readiness and employment opportunities. Support post-graduate employment activities, including job readiness, career navigation, and transition into the workforce. Provide academic advising and individualized student support to promote retention, persistence, and successful completion. Assist students in developing educational and career plans aligned with wellness coaching pathways. Identify and connect students to academic, personal, and professional support resources as needed. Service on committees in the college and university. Assist with tracking graduate outcomes, workforce placement, and post-program success metrics. Review of applications will begin August 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applicants should submit a cover letter of interest describing their teaching philosophy and research agenda, curriculum vita, representative publications, evidence of teaching experience, and a list of three professional references. Selected candidate is expected to obtain licensure in California by tenure. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D./Ed.D./J.D. Doctoral degree in applied psychology or a related field; Licensed or license eligible in CA in an area of applied Psychology or a related field; Demonstrated teaching experience. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in applied psychology Training or expertise in at least one of the following areas: Community Mental Health, Social Work, Child/adolescent mental health, Career Counseling, Telehealth/Technology informed intervention; Applicants who have obtained licensure as in applied psychology; Applicants with expertise in establishing and maintaining internship/practicum sites. Benefits Summary Applicants, please note that actual compensation is determined by several factors that are unique to each candidate, including but not limited to job-related skills, depth of experience, certifications, relevant education or training, and specific work location, among others. The offered wage or salary is only one aspect of an employee’s total compensation Benefits include a comprehensive health and wellness plan, tuition remission program for employee, spouse, and dependent children, a generous contribution to the University’s 403B retirement plan, and a generous time off plan. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and clearance of a background check and employment verification. Location La Verne Main Campus Physical Demands Summary The physical demands include the ability to sit, stand, walk, bend, and lift up to 20 pounds occasionally. Clear verbal and written communication is essential, as the position involves frequent interaction with colleagues, clients, or external partners. The noise level is generally low to moderate. The position may occasionally involve meeting deadlines or managing multiple priorities, which can require sustained focus and mental stamina. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? Yes If yes, list maximum weight and duration 20lbs Describe work environment This position is based in a standard office environment and primarily involves sedentary work. Employees are expected to spend extended periods of time working at a desk, using a computer, and engaging in routine office tasks such as emailing, attending m Duties Salary Range Minimum: $73,585.24 Maximum: $75,117.03 Posting Details Posting Number 2024-250295FA Special Instructions to Applicants The University of La Verne is unable to provide sponsorship for work visas at this time. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for visa sponsorship now or in the future. Open Date 08/31/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? HigherEdjobs.com AcademicCareers.com University of La Verne Website Referred by University of La Verne Employee Other Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
