    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15653": {
      "title": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | FWS -Theatre Technical Student Assistant (26/27)",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | FWS -Theatre Technical Student Assistant (26/27) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FWS -Theatre Technical Student Assistant (26/27) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is an ongoing position which requires reapplication for the first two semesters. However the department is interested training individuals for long term commitments who may be striving for a position that provides leadership experience. Please be ready to articulate how your work in the theatre can benefit the department and how this experience may relate to your future or immediate goals. Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title FWS -Theatre Technical Student Assistant (26/27) Student Position Type Federal Work Study Appointment Type Part-Time FTE Work Schedule Flexible Schedule working weekdays, some evenings and weekends. Ideal candidates can work Monday and Wednesday between 1-4p Department Manager Hiring Manager Alan Tollefson Number of Vacancies 4 Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary Assist with day to day operations of the Theatre Department. Specific Duties Provide support for stagecraft labs, including assisting other students with their work Promote a safe work environment and keep the scene shop clean and orderly Assist faculty with course-related tasks, such as copying and filing Assist with all areas of theatrical production like costumes, painting, building, and warehouse maintenance Help facilitate stagecraft labs and work calls for the scheduled build of theatrical sets and production elements Work along side inexperienced students and help them apply techniques of stagecraft safely within the scheduled time Read plans and follow directives from the Assistant Technical Director and the Technical Director related to building scenic elements and facility/warehouse maintenance Minimum Qualifications Must be a current University of La Verne student with Federal Work Study eligibility for the 2026-2027 academic year Demonstrate a familiarity with some of the tools and techniques related to the theatre such as sewing, painting, drawing, graphic design, carpentry, electrics, computer software, video, or computer programming by providing a letter of recommendation that speaks to the candidates character and experience Preferred Qualifications Experience working backstage on more than one high school or college theatre production Experience completing projects related to building or construction or craft at home or at another institution, or demonstrate through a portfolio or a letter of recommendation, a familiarity with tools and techniques related to the theatre such as sewing, painting, drawing, graphic design, carpentry, electrics, electronics, computer software, video, or computer programming Patience, a sense of humor, and a sincere desire to help others achieve the highest levels of success in technical theatre in order to foster life long learning, diversity, and community building This Role is designed specifically for Student Workers at Junior and Senior status at ULV . Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. Physical Demands Summary The physical demands include the ability to sit, stand, walk, bend, and lift up to 50 pounds occasionally. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? Yes If yes, list maximum weight and duration up to 50 lbs Describe work environment Shop, Backstage and Warehouse Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $18.00 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251586SE Special Instructions to Applicants This is an ongoing position which requires reapplication for the first two semesters. However the department is interested training individuals for long term commitments who may be striving for a position that provides leadership experience. Please be ready to articulate how your work in the theatre can benefit the department and how this experience may relate to your future or immediate goals. Open Date 08/17/2026 Close Date 05/28/2027 Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15649 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a valid California Drivers License? Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? HigherEdjobs.com AcademicCareers.com University of La Verne Website Referred by University of La Verne Employee Other * What experience do you have working on group projects facilitating peer to peer learning? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation 1 Optional Documents University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
