t from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary Perform a variety of supporting duties for the ULV Communications/Digital Media Department, TV and LeoFM station operation. Specific Duties Answer phones, typing, photocopying, running errands, assist in the organization of broadcast office, schedule studio/edit facilities, equipment reservations. Facilitating equipment check in and out procedures. Facilitating studio check in and out procedures. Programming and production assistance. Assist students in radio labs/edit rooms, studio and transmitter maintenance, media organization and cataloging, cleaning and organizing of workroom and studios. LeoFM/Digital Audio and Film/TV studio maintenance and equipment organization, such as charging batteries, equipment checkout, editing bay reservations, labeling equipment and any other functions related to digital media lab/studio operation. Assist faculty and staff as needed. Monitor LVTV’s & LeoFM’s technical quality. Housekeeping duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Must be a current University of La Verne student with Federal Work Study eligibility for the 26/27 academic year. Basic computer skills Able to lift light to heavy objects Ability to work independently Good customer service attitude Hard worker Ability to learn quickly. Must be a current University of La Verne student Preferred Qualifications Film/Radio/TV Equipment knowledge Adobe software knowledge Beginning Radio/Film/TV/Multi-Media Classes ProTools Software Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. Physical Demands Summary The physical demands include the ability to sit, stand, walk, bend, and lift up to 20 pounds occasionally. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? Yes If yes, list maximum weight and duration 100 lbs/ less than a minute Describe work environment Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $16.90 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251544SE Special Instructions to Applicants Open Date 07/01/2026 Close Date 03/01/2027 Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15404 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
