es and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary The Student Assistant will focus on providing administrative support to students, staff, faculty, and administrators of LaFetra College of Education. They will provide support by assisting front office staff with clerical tasks, including answering phones, scheduling appointments, greeting faculty and staff, copying, filing, and general office work. Specific Duties Assist front office staff with clerical tasks, including answering phones, making appointments, greeting and assisting walk-ins, making copies, filing confidential documents, and general office work. Take deliveries across campus, order and maintain office supply inventory, and perform other tasks/duties as assigned. Assist with planning and operation, as well as other event preparation Provide administrative support, guidance, and customer service to program chairs, faculty, students, staff, and other members of the LFCE community Other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Must be a current University of La Verne student with Federal Work Study eligibility for the 26/27 academic year High school diploma Federal Work Study Excellent written and verbal communication MS Office Suite Preferred Qualifications Good customer service skills Good organizational skills Bilingual Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. Physical Demands Summary The physical demands include the ability to sit, stand, walk, bend, lift up to 20 pounds occasionally and Take deliveries across campus. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? Yes If yes, list maximum weight and duration Describe work environment Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $16.90 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251592SE Special Instructions to Applicants Please upload a resume and cover letter Open Date 08/18/2026 Close Date 06/30/2027 Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15667 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 List of 3-5 Professional References University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
