    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15524": {
      "title": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | ASC Success Coach (NFWS) - 2026-2027 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help ASC Success Coach (NFWS) - 2026-2027 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title ASC Success Coach (NFWS) - 2026-2027 Student Position Type Non Federal Work Study/La Verne Work Appointment Type Part-Time FTE Work Schedule We offer flexible work hours, based on the student worker’s availability. This position will require 8 – 10 hours per week. This is an on-campus position. Department Manager Hiring Manager Savannah Garcia, Selena Cordar Number of Vacancies Multiple Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary The Academic Success Center ( ASC ) provides academic support across all majors and disciplines with the goal of helping students become engaged, self-sufficient learners who are confident in their abilities to reach their academic goals. ASC’s Success Coaching program serves all ULV students, helping them to develop skills and habits that aid in personal, professional, and academic success. ASC Success Coaches collaboratively develop individualized coaching plans with students, focusing on goal setting and benchmarks for achievement. Success Coaches also support students on academic probation and reinstatement, incorporating accountability, study strategies, time management, self-organization, and techniques to aid in building self-confidence so students can achieve success and retention in college. Success Coaches work with students individually and in groups, facilitate class visits and workshops, create student resources, and work with ASC professional staff on retention initiatives and outreach. Specific Duties Offer individual coaching appointments, as well as drop-in coaching, to assist students with skills that may be hindering their success, such as time management, achieving balance, goal-setting and accountability, managing academic anxiety, etc. Appointments are held in-person and online within the ASC . Report accurate data for all sessions and service efforts. Collaborate with ASC professional staff and/or campus partners to offer targeted coaching support for distinct student populations (Academic Probation and Reinstatement students, Living Learning Communities, Student Leaders, Accessibility Services, SOS referrals, and faculty/staff referral students.) Develop and facilitate class visits and workshops, as assigned by ASC professional staff, on holistic skills such as goal setting, time management, self organization, study skills, stress management, etc. Develop supplemental materials as assigned by ASC professional staff ( ASC coaching content, student resources, relevant social media posts, events, etc…) Complete supplemental ASC activities, including Coach reflections, observations, co-coaching sessions, trainings, etc. as assigned by ASC professional staff. Other duties as assigned by ASC Director and/or Professional Staff Minimum Qualifications Must be a current ULV student A strong academic background ( minimum overall GPA of 3.25 ). Ability to communicate effectively to help students construct their own understandings of themselves and what habits will help them to be successful. Desire to support peers’ social and emotional wellness, as well as their academic and professional endeavors. Ability to listen to the needs of students and work cooperatively in setting realistic and productive learning goals as well as objectives for reaching those goals. Sensitivity to the diverse socioeconomic, cultural, and academic backgrounds of ASC students Dependability, personal accountability, and the ability to collaborate effectively with others Self-motivation, self-regulation, and a desire to mature and learn in a professional teaching/learning environment Preferred Qualifications Previous academic support experience, particularly in supporting students with documented disabilities Previous tutoring experience Leadership experience and campus involvement Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. Physical Demands Summary The physical demands include the ability to sit, stand, walk, bend, and lift up to 20 pounds occasionally. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? No If yes, list maximum weight and duration Describe work environment Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $16.90 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251542SE Special Instructions to Applicants Open Date 06/02/2026 Close Date 12/31/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15398 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? HigherEdjobs.com AcademicCareers.com University of La Verne Website Referred by University of La Verne Employee Other How do you define success in college? (Open Ended Question) Identify your academic strengths and your experience with overcoming academic challenges. (Open Ended Question) What areas, personally and/or professionally, do you feel you still need further growth and development? (Open Ended Question) Explain why you are interested in this position. (Open Ended Question) What is/was your major field of study? (Open Ended Question) Cumulative GPA? (Open Ended Question) What are the last 4 numbers of your ULV identification number? (Open Ended Question) Do you have another student employment position on campus? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcripts Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
