    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15375": {
      "title": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | Physics Program - Teaching Assistant (Physics Lab) - FWS (2026/2027)",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | Physics Program - Teaching Assistant (Physics Lab) - FWS (2026/2027) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Physics Program - Teaching Assistant (Physics Lab) - FWS (2026/2027) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title Physics Program - Teaching Assistant (Physics Lab) - FWS (2026/2027) Student Position Type Federal Work Study Appointment Type Part-Time FTE Work Schedule TA will work one or two of the following lab sections: Tuesday 02:00 PM – 05:00 PM Tuesday 06:50 PM – 09:50 PM Wednesday 01:00 PM – 04:00 PM Wednesday 06:00 PM – 09:00 PM Thursday 02:00 PM – 05:00 PM Thursday 06:50 PM – 09:50 PM Mandatory Pre-Lab Meetings: Fridays (time to be decided) Attend mandatory weekly pre-lab meetings. Department Manager Hiring Manager Jignesh Patel Number of Vacancies 10 Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary Lab instructors will rely on their teaching assistants to provide valuable instructional/grading support and offer their unique insights for improving the labs from a student perspective. While helping fellow students learn physics, teaching assistants will become better teachers, better learners, better communicators, and improve their own understanding of physics. Specific Duties Teaching assistants will: Use technology to assist students in completing their physics labs. Help students to safely and effectively use specialized scientific apparatuses, computerized data acquisition systems, and data analysis techniques. Facilitate small group interactions and deep discussions about theoretical and experimental physics phenomena. Assist instructors with conceptual introductions, troubleshooting equipment malfunctions, and grading as necessary. Attend mandatory weekly pre-lab meetings. Minimum Qualifications Must be current University of La Verne student. Successful completion of the Physics sequence 201/203 or 202/204 with a grade of B- or better. Interest in physical science. Preferred Qualifications Committed to working both Fall and Spring semesters for a minimum of 5 hours/week. Ability to communicate effectively and help students construct their own understandings of lab material. Dependable, reliable, and self-sufficient. Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. Physical Demands Summary The physical demands include the ability to sit, stand, walk, bend, and lift up to 20 pounds occasionally. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? No If yes, list maximum weight and duration Describe work environment Physics Laboratory Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $16.90 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251533SE Special Instructions to Applicants Open Date 06/01/2026 Close Date 06/01/2027 Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15341 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is/was your major field of study? (Open Ended Question) Anticipated Graduation Date? (Open Ended Question) Cumulative GPA? (Open Ended Question) What is your award amount for your Federal Work Study? (Open Ended Question) * Are you a current student of the University of La Verne? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter Resume University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15652": {
      "title": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | NFWS Theatre Technical Assistant 26/27",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | NFWS Theatre Technical Assistant 26/27 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help NFWS Theatre Technical Assistant 26/27 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is an ongoing position for graduate students which requires reapplication for the first two semesters. However the department is interested in training individuals for long term commitments who may be striving for a position that provides leadership experience. Please be ready to articulate how your work in the theatre can benefit the department and how this experience may relate to your future or immediate goals. Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title NFWS Theatre Technical Assistant 26/27 Student Position Type Non Federal Work Study/La Verne Work Appointment Type Part-Time FTE Work Schedule Flexible Schedule working weekdays, some evenings and weekends. Ideal candidates can work Monday and Wednesday between 1-4p. Department Manager Hiring Manager Alan Tollefson Number of Vacancies 6 Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary Assist with day to day operations of the department. Specific Duties Provide support for stagecraft labs, including assisting other students with their work. Promote a safe work environment and keep the scene shop clean and orderly. Assist faculty with course-related tasks, such as copying and filing. Assist with all areas of theatrical production like costumes, painting, building, and warehouse maintenance. Help facilitate stagecraft labs and work calls for the scheduled build of theatrical sets and production elements. Work along side inexperienced students and help them apply techniques of stagecraft safely within the scheduled time. Read plans and follow directives from the Assistant Technical Director and the Technical Director related to building scenic elements and facility/warehouse maintenance. Minimum Qualifications Must be a current University of La Verne Graduate student Demonstrate a familiarity with some of the tools and techniques related to the theatre such as sewing, painting, drawing, graphic design, carpentry, electrics, computer software, video, or computer programming by providing a letter of recommendation that speaks to the candidates character and experience. Preferred Qualifications Experience working backstage on more than one high school or college theatre production. Experience completing projects related to building or construction or craft at home or at another institution, or demonstrate through a portfolio or a letter of recommendation, a familiarity with tools and techniques related to the theatre such as sewing, painting, drawing, graphic design, carpentry, electrics, electronics, computer software, video, or computer programming. Patience, a sense of humor, and a sincere desire to help others achieve the highest levels of success in technical theatre in order to foster life long learning, diversity, and community building. Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. Physical Demands Summary The physical demands include the ability to sit, stand, walk, bend, and lift up to 50 pounds occasionally. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? Yes If yes, list maximum weight and duration Short lifts up to 50lbs. Describe work environment Shop, Backstage and Warehouse Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $16.90 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251585SE Special Instructions to Applicants This is an ongoing position for graduate students which requires reapplication for the first two semesters. However the department is interested in training individuals for long term commitments who may be striving for a position that provides leadership experience. Please be ready to articulate how your work in the theatre can benefit the department and how this experience may relate to your future or immediate goals. Open Date 08/17/2026 Close Date 05/28/2027 Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15648 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a valid California Drivers License? Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? HigherEdjobs.com AcademicCareers.com University of La Verne Website Referred by University of La Verne Employee Other * What experience do you have working on group projects facilitating peer to peer learning? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation 1 Optional Documents University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15528": {
      "title": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | ASC Tutor (FWS) 2026-2027 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help ASC Tutor (FWS) 2026-2027 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title ASC Tutor (FWS) 2026-2027 Student Position Type Federal Work Study Appointment Type Part-Time FTE Work Schedule Work schedule varies; a minimum of 5 hours per week Department Manager Hiring Manager Savannah Garcia, Selena Cordar Number of Vacancies Multiple Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary During individual and group settings, ASC Tutors work with students on learning and retaining content and material in their assigned subject areas. ASC Tutors utilize learning strategies during their sessions to help students understand their course material, offering supplemental support and encouraging student autonomy as necessary. ASC Tutors also facilitate class visits to increase student utilization of ASC services, facilitate events relevant to their subject areas, develop academic resources, and contribute to ASC strategic efforts to enhance student learning and access to educational support. ASC Tutors may also support students and faculty in the classroom, offering individualized attention to students, assisting with classroom activities, and offering supplemental group tutoring sessions outside the classroom to aid in student learning and content retention. Specific Duties Conduct face-to-face, online, asynchronous, and/or drop-in tutoring sessions in assigned subject area(s) with students both individually and in groups, helping students develop their own best practices for becoming self-sufficient learners. Gather and report accurate data for each student, service effort, and/or tutoring session. Attend and actively participate in all mandatory trainings and meetings, including orientation; onboarding; weekly meetings; online workshops; and/or other relevant trainings required for specific subjects or focus areas (e.g. group facilitation methods for those offering group sessions, research strategies for those offering research support, etc.) Complete supplemental ASC activities, including ASC class visits, tutor reflections, observations, co-tutoring sessions, special projects, etc. as assigned by ASC professional staff. Review and create academic resources available through the ASC , referring students to resource materials and/or staff members based on their individual needs and ability levels. Other duties as assigned by the Director and/or ASC professional staff. Minimum Qualifications A strong academic background ( minimum overall undergraduate GPA of 3.25 ) Ability to communicate effectively to help students construct their own understandings of course/subject materials Ability to listen to the needs of students and work cooperatively in setting realistic and productive learning goals Sensitivity to the diverse socioeconomic, cultural, and academic backgrounds of ASC students Dependability and personal accountability Self-motivation, self-regulation, and a desire to mature and learn in a professionalteaching/learning environment Preferred Qualifications Ability to apply growth learning, self-regulated learning, scaffolding, metacognition,and similar learning strategies in tutoring practice. Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. Physical Demands Summary The physical demands include the ability to sit, stand, walk, bend, and lift up to 20 pounds occasionally. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? No If yes, list maximum weight and duration Describe work environment Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $16.90 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251547SE Special Instructions to Applicants Open Date 06/02/2026 Close Date 12/31/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15414 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? HigherEdjobs.com AcademicCareers.com University of La Verne Website Referred by University of La Verne Employee Other What is/was your major field of study? (Open Ended Question) Cumulative GPA? (Open Ended Question) Anticipated Graduation Date? (Open Ended Question) Name of faculty member for departmental recommendation. (Open Ended Question) Briefly explain the qualifications you believe will make you an effective tutor. (Open Ended Question) In what subject area(s) are you applying to tutor? (Open Ended Question) Do you still need an LVHU attribute for your degree program?\r\n*Please note: If you do need an LVHU attribute - and are hired as an ASC Tutor - you will be asked to register for RCS 270, which is a peer tutoring course being offered this fall. YES NO Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcripts Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
