    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/14275": {
      "title": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | Accessibility Services Student Assistant (2025/2026) - FWS",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | Accessibility Services Student Assistant (2025/2026) - FWS Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Accessibility Services Student Assistant (2025/2026) - FWS Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title Accessibility Services Student Assistant (2025/2026) - FWS Student Position Type Federal Work Study Appointment Type Part-Time FTE Work Schedule 10-15 hours per week. Student schedule must be flexible to work between Monday-Friday 8 am-5 pm. Department Manager Hiring Manager Lisa Lester Number of Vacancies Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary Responsible for proctoring exams for students registered with Accessibility Services at the University of La Verne, coordinating proctoring schedule, processing proctor-related forms and test accommodation documents, and assisting with other aspects of Accessibility Services. Specific Duties Proctoring exams for students registered with Accessibility Services. Coordinating proctor and exam list schedule. Assisting with Accessibility Services programming efforts. Assist in creating flyers/newsletter and general marketing of Accessibility Services to students and faculty/staff. Track data and usage of accommodations across campuses, assist in implementation of workshops related to test taking strategies etc. Organizing, sorting, processing paperwork, and/or copying materials. Collecting and tracking data on student communications, interactions, and success strategies. Assisting Accessibility Services department in various projects and initiatives. Monitoring and notifying the Director of Accessibility Services of any escalated issues. Performing additional duties as assigned, including other administrative duties. Minimum Qualifications A dependable, computer proficient student who is able to follow directions and complete assigned work in a timely manner. Must be able and willing to handle data and material in a confidential manner. Excellent phone etiquette, listening and communication skills. Proficient in Excel, Microsoft Word, Outlook and Google Drive. Must be a ULV student Preferred Qualifications Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. Physical Demands Summary Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? If yes, list maximum weight and duration Describe work environment Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $16.90 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251410SE Special Instructions to Applicants Open Date 06/11/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/14266 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
