    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15550": {
      "title": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | FWS - Fraternity &amp; Sorority Life Student Assistant (2026/2027)",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | FWS - Fraternity &amp; Sorority Life Student Assistant (2026/2027) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FWS - Fraternity & Sorority Life Student Assistant (2026/2027) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title FWS - Fraternity & Sorority Life Student Assistant (2026/2027) Student Position Type Federal Work Study Appointment Type Part-Time FTE Work Schedule Office hours are Monday through Friday 8AM-5PM with occasional changes for events. Schedule is dependent on students’ availability and Federal Work Study award. Student employees will work an average of 5 to 11 hours per week. Department Manager Hiring Manager Number of Vacancies 1 Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary Assist the Office of Student Engagement and Leadership staff as the Fraternity and Sorority Life Student Lead. The main purpose of the Fraternity and Sorority Life Lead is to promote and gain exposure for the Fraternity and Sorority Life Community. Specific Duties Create and distribute marketing materials, send bi-weekly Fraternity and Sorority Life Newsletter, and assist with other program support materials for Fraternity and Sorority Life. (35%) Assist with planning and execution of but not limited to meetings, Involvement Fair, Fraternity and Sorority Life Conference, Fraternity and Sorority Life Week, Fraternity and Sorority Life New Member Orientation, Office of Student Engagement and Leadership Award Ceremony, and other important programming. (30%) Attend weekly meetings with the Office of Student Engagement and Leadership Coordinator. (15%) Assist with administrative duties (i.e. check email account, making copies, etc.) (15%) Maintain a clean and organized Fraternity and Sorority Life Student Lead workspace. (5%) Minimum Qualifications Meet and maintain a 2.0 GPA for the semester and cumulative Positive attitude and friendly Must be an initiated member of a ULV -recognized social fraternity or sorority Organization and time management Must be comfortable and capable of interacting and speaking in public settings and facilitating meetings Must be a current ULV student. Preferred Qualifications Ability to know, understand and work with University of La Verne policies and procedures Good oral and written communication skills Develop spreadsheets and PowerPoint presentations Good oral and written communication skills Experience utilizing Canva, MailChimp, and other design platforms Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. Physical Demands Summary The physical demands include the ability to sit, stand, walk, bend, and lift up to 20 pounds occasionally. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? No If yes, list maximum weight and duration Describe work environment Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $17.40 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251567SE Special Instructions to Applicants Open Date 07/01/2026 Close Date 09/30/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15546 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
