    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/14864": {
      "title": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | REACH Day Counselor - June 2026 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help REACH Day Counselor - June 2026 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Must apply on-line Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title REACH Day Counselor - June 2026 Student Position Type Non Federal Work Study/La Verne Work Appointment Type Temporary FTE Work Schedule Up to 28 hours per week Sunday 6/7/2026 through Friday 6/26/2026. M-F 8:00AM through 5:00PM. Must also be available some weekends & special events. Students enrolled in summer courses can only work up to 20 hours per week. Department Manager Hiring Manager Issam Ghazzawi Number of Vacancies Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary Approximately 6 positions available. Counselor to high school students. Help with classwork. Must be with them during hours of work schedule with some exceptions. Specific Duties Must be able to help students with business related questions. Escort students during hours of work schedule. Chaperoning during field trips during the day. Maintain order. Minimum Qualifications Current ULV student recommended by Dr. Ghazzawi and/or a prof. from the integrated program. Business major/minor. Preferred Qualifications Current ENACTUS student. Previous REACH Counselor and/or REACH student and/or in the integrated program. Must be a current La Verne Student for Fall 2026. Spring 2027 graduates are not eligible. Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. Physical Demands Summary Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? If yes, list maximum weight and duration Describe work environment Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $17.40 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251493SE Special Instructions to Applicants Must apply on-line Open Date 02/12/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/14862 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is/was your major field of study? (Open Ended Question) * Are you in good academic standing? yes no * Cumulative GPA? (Open Ended Question) * Anticipated Graduation Date? (Open Ended Question) * Major / Degree Program? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Transcripts Letter of Recommendation 1 University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15674": {
      "title": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | FWSCS (Fairplex) Learning and Development Center CTEC Assistant (26/27) - FWS Only",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | FWSCS (Fairplex) Learning and Development Center CTEC Assistant (26/27) - FWS Only Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FWSCS (Fairplex) Learning and Development Center CTEC Assistant (26/27) - FWS Only Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title FWSCS (Fairplex) Learning and Development Center CTEC Assistant (26/27) - FWS Only Student Position Type Federal Work Study Appointment Type Part-Time FTE Work Schedule Work Schedule: The Federal Work Study CTEC Assistant will work between 8-20 hours per week on a schedule agreed upon with the College and Career Services Counselor (may include occasional evenings or weekends). Students must have reliable transportation to and from work site. Department Manager Hiring Manager Myrna Hugo Number of Vacancies 2 Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary * IMPORTANT NOTE : APPLICANTS MUST be currently enrolled at ULV and have a FEDERAL WORK STUDY award to be eligible for this position. * The Career and Technical Education Center ( CTEC ) Assistant will support the College and Career Services Counselor and CTEC staff with general office duties, program coordination, and student engagement. This position plays a key role in ensuring the smooth operation of CTEC’s pathways and services, contributing to the success of the program and its students. The starting pay for this position is $18.00 per hour. Specific Duties · Perform general office tasks such as filing, data entry, photocopying, and organizing materials. · Maintain records of student attendance, workshop participation, and event sign-ups. · Assist in preparing and distributing materials for workshops and events. · Set up and organize classrooms or meeting spaces, including event materials like name tags and sign-in sheets. · Support event logistics, including managing registration and guiding participants. · Help coordinate student events, including workshops, mock interviews, and orientation sessions. · Provide administrative support during presentations and workshops. · Work collaboratively with staff to complete tasks and projects on time.Follow safety and confidentiality guidelines to ensure a professional environment. · Research and compile information on grants, scholarships, internships, job opportunities, apprenticeships, and other career, educational, and funding opportunities to support students and programs. · Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Must be a current University of La Verne student with Federal Work Study eligibility for the 2025-2026 academic year. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Proficiency in basic computer applications (e.g., Microsoft Office, Google Suite). Ability to handle confidential information responsibly. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Must be able to multitask and work in a dynamic environment. Willingness to assist in various tasks as needed, including occasional evening or weekend events. Ability to stand, sit, and lift up to 20 lbs occasionally. Must have reliable transportation to/from work site. Preferred Qualifications The ideal CTEC Assistant is organized, detail-oriented, and proactive in supporting the day-to-day operations of CTEC . They should have excellent communication skills, a positive attitude, and a willingness to learn. This candidate is enthusiastic about education and enjoys interacting with students, staff, and community members. Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location Other If Other, please specify. 1101 W. McKinley Ave. Pomona, CA 91768 Physical Demands Summary Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? Yes If yes, list maximum weight and duration 20lbs occassionally Describe work environment Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate Other Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251593SE Special Instructions to Applicants Open Date 08/21/2026 Close Date 10/31/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15671 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
