    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15609": {
      "title": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | Human Resources Student Assistant (26/27) - FWS Only",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | Human Resources Student Assistant (26/27) - FWS Only Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Student Assistant (26/27) - FWS Only Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title Human Resources Student Assistant (26/27) - FWS Only Student Position Type Federal Work Study Appointment Type Regular FTE Work Schedule The Office of Human Resources is open 8AM-5PM, Monday through Friday. Student employees will provide the supervisor with their class schedule each semester. The supervisor will build the work schedule based on the submitted class schedules. Department Manager Hiring Manager Vanessa Covey Number of Vacancies 1 Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary The Human Resources Student Assistant will provide administrative support across all divisions of the Office of Human Resources at the University. This entry level position provides an introduction to different areas of Human Resources such as Talent Management, Payroll, Benefits, Compensation, and HRIS . This position plays a critical role in covering the front desk area of the office and often serves as the first point of contact for faculty, staff, students, vendors, community partners, and other guests. Specific Duties Front desk area coverage, when needed, for the office. Tasks may include: Greeting visitors and directing them to the appropriate staff member for assistance. Answering phone calls for the general Human Resources office phone number. Taking and delivering messages. Opening, sorting, and distributing mail/deliveries. Supports the Office of Human Resources with special projects such as: Maintaining the Position Description Questionnaire database Maintaining the Organizational Charts database Preparing agendas for Talent Management Team meetings Editing forms and templates for the HR Portal. Other projects. Projects are assigned based on the HR Student Assistant’s skill set and work schedule. Projects can change each semester. Prepare check requests, invoices, and other financial/business forms to be reviewed and signed off by Human Resources staff and then delivered to the Office of Financial and Business Services for processing Other duties as assigned by the Talent Management Coordinator for Student Employment. HR Student Assistants frequently help with a variety of ad hoc tasks and projects as needed for all divisions of Human Resources Minimum Qualifications Must be a current University of La Verne student with Federal Work Study eligibility for the 2026-2027 academic year. Previous customer service experience. Demonstrated interpersonal, organizational, time management, and prioritization skills. Demonstrated attention to details and accuracy. Must maintain a high level of confidentiality. Preferred Qualifications Interest in Human Resources and/or Business Management as a career path. Majoring in Business Administration, Business Management, or Leadership and Management. Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. Park Campus is located 1 mile away from main campus Physical Demands Summary The physical demands include the ability to sit, stand, walk, bend, and lift up to 20 pounds occasionally. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? No If yes, list maximum weight and duration Describe work environment Office Setting Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $16.90 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251572SE Special Instructions to Applicants Open Date 08/01/2025 Close Date 10/01/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15591 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is your availability for the upcoming semester? Please consider your class schedule and extracurricular activities. (Open Ended Question) Are you a current student at the University of La Verne (any ULV Campus or ULV Online Classes)? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcripts Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 List of 3-5 Professional References University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
