    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15618": {
      "title": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | FWS Football Film Coordinator - SA I (FWS ONLY) 26-27",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | FWS Football Film Coordinator - SA I (FWS ONLY) 26-27 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FWS Football Film Coordinator - SA I (FWS ONLY) 26-27 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete entire application with your university information, including your banner ID (student ID), student email, and FWS award. Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title FWS Football Film Coordinator - SA I (FWS ONLY) 26-27 Student Position Type Federal Work Study Appointment Type Part-Time FTE Work Schedule Seasonal Work Schedule will be Tuesday – Sunday August to November & or February – March. Work 18 – 20 hours per week. Department Manager Jenna Panatier Hiring Manager John Roberts Number of Vacancies 3 Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary The Athletics Film Coordinator – Football is responsible for all aspects of football film operations at the University of La Verne. This includes filming practices and games, editing and uploading footage, maintaining film equipment, and operating the team’s replay system. The coordinator plays a critical role in supporting the coaching staff’s preparation and in-game decision-making by ensuring accurate, timely, and organized film resources. Under the supervision of the Head Football Coach and Athletics Director, the Football Film Coordinator films all practices and games, edits and organizes footage for coaching review, operates and maintains the replay system during games, and ensures all film equipment is properly maintained. The coordinator also assists with broader game day operations as needed. Specific Duties Filming – Practices & Games – Film all football practices and home/away games from assigned angles. Ensure complete and uninterrupted coverage of all plays from snap to whistle. 45% Film Upload & Organization – Upload game and practice film to the team’s film platform in a timely manner following each session. Label, tag, and organize footage by date, type (practice/game), and play category as directed by coaching staff. 15% Film Editing – Edit game and practice film to produce cut-ups, highlight clips, and opponent scouting reels as directed. Use designated video software to trim, annotate, and compile clips for coaching review. 15% Replay System Operation – Set up and operate the iPad-based replay system during games and practice. Connect iPad(s) to the replay system and ensure real-time video is accessible to coaches on the sideline and in the press box. 10% Equipment Maintenance & Setup – Maintain, transport, and set up all film equipment including cameras, tripods, tablets, cables, and charging stations. Conduct pre-game and pre-practice equipment checks. Report any damaged or malfunctioning equipment to the supervisor promptly. 10% Other Duties as Assigned – Assist with additional game day operations, special projects, or media duties as directed by the coaching staff or Athletics department. 5% Minimum Qualifications A. Education / Degrees Required: High School Diploma or GED (enrolled ULV student) B. Required Minimum Experience: Basic knowledge of football (rules, positions, and play structure) Experience operating a video camera, DSLR , or mobile recording device Ability to lift and transport equipment (minimum 25 lbs.) Good communication skills and the ability to follow detailed instructions Willingness to learn new software and technology tools Punctuality and reliability; must be available for all scheduled practices and games C. Required Minimum Knowledge and Skills: Familiarity with video recording equipment (cameras, tripods, stabilizers) Basic computer skills, including file management and cloud storage Ability to operate an iPad and connect to external devices/systems Organizational skills to manage and label large volumes of video files Ability to work independently and under time pressure on game days Preferred Qualifications Experience with video editing software (Hudl, Krossover, Adobe Premiere, iMovie, or similar) Prior experience filming or working in a sports film/media role Familiarity with iPad-based replay systems (e.g., Coach’s Eye, XOS , or similar) Working knowledge of football offensive and defensive schemes Experience uploading and organizing footage on film platforms (Hudl, XOS , etc.) Strong verbal communication skills are required for real-time coordination with coaching staff. Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. University of La Verne Athletics Facilities Physical Demands Summary This position requires the ability to stand and walk for extended periods during practices and games (up to 3–4 hours), lift and carry equipment weighing up to 40 lbs., work outdoors in variable weather conditions, climb stairs or elevated filming platforms, and perform repetitive hand/arm movements while operating cameras and tablets. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? Yes If yes, list maximum weight and duration 40ibs lift and carry Describe work environment Outdoors in variable waether conditions Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $16.90 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251511SE Special Instructions to Applicants Please complete entire application with your university information, including your banner ID (student ID), student email, and FWS award. Open Date 05/01/2025 Close Date 09/30/2027 Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15225 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you able to perform the required essential functions related to this position? YES NO Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15268": {
      "title": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | FWS - Student Assistant, Student Outreach and Support (2026/2027)",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | FWS - Student Assistant, Student Outreach and Support (2026/2027) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FWS - Student Assistant, Student Outreach and Support (2026/2027) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title FWS - Student Assistant, Student Outreach and Support (2026/2027) Student Position Type Federal Work Study Appointment Type Part-Time FTE Work Schedule This is a part-time, up to 20 hours per week, position with some events, workshops, and meetings. The weekly work schedule is flexible with regular supervisor check-ins. Department Manager Hiring Manager Ebony Williams Number of Vacancies Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary Students in this role will focus on promoting student well-being both inside and outside of the classroom. This SOS team of work study students will present SOS services in the classroom, at campus fairs and events and on social media. This team will also develop social media content and digital wellness material, be the voice of the student body regarding relevant workshop content, and support the delivery of workshops on campus. Specific Duties With the guidance of the SOS fellow, this team will research the wellness needs of the student body, determine the most effective methods for meeting those needs, and advise the SOS manager regarding future programming efforts. Under the direction of the social media manager, team members will plan, create, and post SOS related social media content to the @ulvcares social media account. This team will plan, coordinate, staff and assess all SOS tabling and event participation, including Wellness Wednesdays, club fairs, and Spotlight weekend. Team members will meet weekly to discuss progress, provide support and celebrate impact made on campus. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications You should be one of the following: A curious researcher who likes discovering and reporting new information. An outgoing personality that enjoys connecting with and speaking to others. A creative individual who enjoys graphic design and or event planning. You believe everyone deserves to be well and would like to help your peers achieve wellness. You work to build diversity, equity, inclusion, belonging, and justice in your sphere of influence. Preferred Qualifications Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. Physical Demands Summary Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? If yes, list maximum weight and duration Describe work environment Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $16.90 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251510SE Special Instructions to Applicants Open Date 04/29/2026 Close Date 05/24/2027 Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15263 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15499": {
      "title": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | Organic Chemistry Lab Student Teaching Assistant I NFWS (26/27)",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | Organic Chemistry Lab Student Teaching Assistant I NFWS (26/27) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Organic Chemistry Lab Student Teaching Assistant I NFWS (26/27) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. If you have not been a TA before, you will need to meet with the department to fill out an additional form regarding any other Science and Math courses you have taken so far. Unofficial transcripts or screen captures of your Grade for the Course you will be a TA for is fine. Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title Organic Chemistry Lab Student Teaching Assistant I NFWS (26/27) Student Position Type Non Federal Work Study/La Verne Work Appointment Type Part-Time FTE Work Schedule Position could start as early as the week of August 10th for any needed trainings. Fall 2026 lab sections, which meet beginning 8/24/26, are as follows: Mon    1:00PM – 5:10PM Tues    6:00PM – 10:10PM Wed    1:00PM – 5:10PM Thurs  1:00PM – 5:10PM Thurs  6:00PM – 10:10PM Mandatory Weekly Lab Meeting (Day and Time to be decided) This position will work 100% on campus. Department Manager Hiring Manager Andrew Rice Number of Vacancies 6 Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary This is a student teaching assistant position for currently enrolled students at the University of La Verne. Lab TA’s will assist the instructor in the proper functioning of the lab during the session and help students follow proper techniques and safety rules while conducting experiments. TA’s must be proactive in the lab and model proper laboratory safety at all times, including wearing the proper protective equipment: lab coats, goggles and proper clothing and shoes. This position may be extended to the Spring 2026semester after evaluation by the lab coordinator on performance in the lab. Specific Duties Teaching assistants will: Come prepared and on time or earlier to their respective lab with proper PPE and with knowledge of the experiment and ready to answer student’s questions. Must attend the weekly lab meetings. TA must remain proactive in labs and observe/keep an eye on students to ensure that they are following proper laboratory techniques and safety. They must remain vigilant at all times and keep an eye on the student’s use of the chemicals during the experiments to prevent or catch cross contamination. TAs must communicate with the Lab instructors / Lab Coordinators / Lab Managers regarding any concerns with the chemicals or lab safety. Ensure the Maintenance of the lab’s cleanliness during their respective lab and conduct lab clean up (putting away equipment or cleaning glassware, keep chemicals in order, etc.), and sometimes help set up (prepare waste containers or pipettes, help with preparation of chemicals, etc.) Grade assignments within a reasonable turnaround time Minimum Qualifications Successful completion of CHEM 311/312 with a grade of B- or better. Mandatory attendance at the weekly lab meetings. Committed to working both Fall and Spring semesters for a minimum of 10 hours/week. Must be a current University of La Verne student Preferred Qualifications Recommendation from a Chemistry instructor Driven and takes initiative Ability to communicate effectively Basic knowledge of Excel Dependable, reliable, and self-sufficient Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. Physical Demands Summary The physical demands include the ability to sit, stand, walk, bend, and lift up to 20 pounds occasionally. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? No If yes, list maximum weight and duration Describe work environment Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $16.90 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251561SE Special Instructions to Applicants If you have not been a TA before, you will need to meet with the department to fill out an additional form regarding any other Science and Math courses you have taken so far. Unofficial transcripts or screen captures of your Grade for the Course you will be a TA for is fine. Open Date 06/22/2026 Close Date 06/30/2027 Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15494 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Did you pass Organic Chemistry I and II (CHEM 311 and 312) with at least a B- at ULV? Yes Yes, but not at ULV Only for CHEM 311 No Applicant Documents Required Documents Transcripts Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15631": {
      "title": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | FWSCS La Verne Parent Participation Preschool (LVPPP)  - Teacher&#39;s Aide (26/27) - FWS Only Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FWSCS La Verne Parent Participation Preschool (LVPPP)  - Teacher's Aide (26/27) - FWS Only Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title FWSCS La Verne Parent Participation Preschool (LVPPP)  - Teacher's Aide (26/27) - FWS Only Student Position Type Federal Work Study Appointment Type Part-Time FTE Work Schedule This part-time position is available for 4-20 hours per week of in-person work at La Verne Parent Participation Preschool. Schedule is flexible (within the hours of Monday through Friday from 8:30am to 12:30pm), in consultation with the Director. Some weekend and evening hours may be available intermittently for special events. Students must have reliable transportation to and from LVPPP in La Verne. Department Manager Hiring Manager Myrna Hugo Number of Vacancies 1 Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary * IMPORTANT NOTE : APPLICANTS MUST be currently enrolled at ULV and have a FEDERAL WORK STUDY award to be eligible for this position. * La Verne Parent Participation Preschool ( LVPPP ) is a non-profit, non-discriminatory family organization owned and operated by member families in the co-op tradition. Our mission is to create a thriving early childhood education program that deeply respects and nurtures the potential that exists in each individual child, teacher, and family. We strive to create an environment rich in respect, individuality, and that celebrates diversity. Our unique program provides a strong foundation for learning, and actively engages families and the community to provide a positive and nurturing learning environment for each child. LVPPP is looking for a Teacher’s Aide who can support Teachers in developing curriculum and caring for children, ages 2 through 6. Under the supervision of the Director and in close collaboration with the Teachers, the Aide may provide classroom support, including setting up age-appropriate learning stations and engaging students in educational activities. The starting pay for this position is $17.00 per hour. Specific Duties The Teacher’s Aide will report directly to the Director and work closely with the preschool Teachers. All tasks will be performed under the guidance and direction of the Teacher or Director at all times and may include: • Supervising children ages 2 to 6 years old and interacting with families in a professional and courteous manner • Assisting teachers with creating and facilitating developmentally appropriate curriculum • Addressing children’s physical, emotional, social and academic needs as appropriate • Aiding teachers in documenting children’s progress and development • Setting up, organizing and cleaning classroom and outdoor spaces to provide a safe learning environment as needed • Organizing and managing the school’s early childhood library • Participating in staff and board meetings and supporting special events as appropriate Minimum Qualifications Must be a current University of La Verne student with Federal Work Study eligibility for the 2026-2027 academic year. Engage with children and their families Employ strong customer service, organization, verbal/written communication, and problem-solving skills Listen carefully, follow directions, and think critically Work collaboratively on a team Maintain a positive attitude and a strong desire to learn Preferred Qualifications The ideal candidate demonstrates: • Demonstrates some knowledge of early childhood education • Desires to learn more about early childhood development • Has experience in working with children and families • Exhibits creativity and resourcefulness • Takes initiative and is a self-starter Bilingual applicants encouraged to apply. Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location Other If Other, please specify. 909 East Juanita Avenue, La Verne, California 91750 Physical Demands Summary The physical demands include the ability to sit, stand, walk, bend, and lift up to 20 pounds occasionally. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? No If yes, list maximum weight and duration Describe work environment Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate Other Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251580SE Special Instructions to Applicants Open Date 07/31/2026 Close Date 10/30/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15626 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
