    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15299": {
      "title": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | Athletics Game Management - FWS Only (2026/2027) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Athletics Game Management - FWS Only (2026/2027) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete entire application with your university information, including your banner ID (student ID), student email, and FWS award. Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title Athletics Game Management - FWS Only (2026/2027) Student Position Type Federal Work Study Appointment Type Regular FTE Work Schedule Coordinates with ULV Athletics home competitions and other special events. Schedule is most active on weekends, and availability on Saturdays during the fall season is essential. Works 5-15 hours per week. Department Manager Jenna Panatier Hiring Manager Ebony Turner Number of Vacancies 80-100 Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary Student employees in the Game Management department are tasked with a range of responsibilities related to hosting home intercollegiate athletic events. These duties include assisting with the preparation and disassembly of facilities and equipment for sporting competitions, as well as managing various aspects of game day operations such as field maintenance, in-game management, community engagement, photography, videography, multimedia design, and marketing. Leadership opportunities are also available for students in supervisory roles. Specific Duties Attend mandatory orientation and scheduled job trainings. Saturdays will be required shifts during the fall season so please plan accordingly. Student workers will be trained in all positions for each season. GM positions include but are not limited to: officiate stats keeping, shot clock and scoreboard (training provided), PA announcer, on field/court crew, video production, live stream, video record, play by play broadcasting, photography, multimedia design, marketing team, fan experience team. Seasonal sports include; football, soccer, volleyball, cross country, golf, basketball, swim and dive, water polo, baseball, softball and track and field. Minimum Qualifications Must be a current University of La Verne student. Must have a FWS award for the current academic year. Basic knowledge of sports and sports equipment. Ability to lift and transport equipment. Good communication skills and willingness to learn new skills. Demonstrated awareness and commitment to effectively establishing relationships and positive communications across multiple dimensions of diversity including, but not limited to race, gender, sexual preference/identity, physical limitations, class or religious perspectives. Ability to work with a diverse team in a fast-paced environment. Enthusiasm and the ability to thrive in an atmosphere of constant change. Preferred Qualifications Willingness to learn sporting rules and guidelines. Previous experience with athletics and game day operations. Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. University of La Verne Athletics Facilities Physical Demands Summary The physical demands include the ability to sit, stand, walk, bend, and lift up to 20 pounds occasionally. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? Yes If yes, list maximum weight and duration Ability to lift and transport sporting equipment Describe work environment Athletics / Outdoor and Indoor Sporting Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $16.90 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251520SE Special Instructions to Applicants Please complete entire application with your university information, including your banner ID (student ID), student email, and FWS award. Open Date 05/01/2026 Close Date 06/30/2027 Open Until Filled No Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15297 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). When is your first available day of work? (Open Ended Question) What days and times are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15719": {
      "title": "Fitness Instructor (26/27)",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | Fitness Instructor (26/27) - NFWS Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Fitness Instructor (26/27) - NFWS Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title Fitness Instructor (26/27) - NFWS Student Position Type Non Federal Work Study/La Verne Work Appointment Type Part-Time FTE Work Schedule Classes may occur during the following hours, but will work with instructor’s schedule: Monday – Thursday 7a – 11p Fri 7a- 7p Department Manager Hiring Manager Allison Krich Number of Vacancies multiple Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary The Fitness Instructor is responsible for leading movement classes at the Randall Lewis Center for Well-Being and Research. This is a non-federal work study position, but will consider those with federal work study also. Please apply. Specific Duties Instruct fitness and well-being classes Record attendance Provide a safe environment for participants Minimum Qualifications Experience instructing others in movement required. Preferably traditional group fitness and/or dance classes (i.e. yoga, pilates, dance, hip-hop, HIIT , etc) Yoga instructors must be certified Good communication skills Excellent customer service Must be a ULV student Preferred Qualifications 1 year experience leading movement classes with preference to those who have a group exercise certification CPR / AED certified preferred but not required at hire Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. Physical Demands Summary The physical demands include the ability to sit, stand, walk, bend, and lift up to 20 pounds occasionally. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? No If yes, list maximum weight and duration Describe work environment Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $16.90 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251596SE Special Instructions to Applicants Open Date 09/04/2026 Close Date 11/04/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15718 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
