    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15751": {
      "title": "FWS- Undergraduate Assistant, Leo Food Pantry (2026/2027)",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | FWS- Undergraduate Assistant, Leo Food Pantry (2026/2027) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help FWS- Undergraduate Assistant, Leo Food Pantry (2026/2027) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title FWS- Undergraduate Assistant, Leo Food Pantry (2026/2027) Student Position Type Federal Work Study Appointment Type Part-Time FTE Work Schedule This part-time, up to 20 hours per week, position works regularly scheduled hours in the Leo Food Pantry, with occasional work off campus. Department Manager Hiring Manager Ebony Williams Number of Vacancies 1 Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary The Leo Food Pantry Undergraduate Assistant serves as a student ambassador for the Leo Food Pantry, helping to increase awareness of pantry services, reduce stigma associated with accessing basic needs resources, and strengthen connections between the Pantry and the University of La Verne community. This position plays a critical role in promoting food security initiatives, helping students learn about available resources, supporting pantry operations, and coordinating donation focused events. This position is designed to provide students with hands-on experience in community engagement, event planning, communications, and nonprofit operations. Undergraduate Assistants work closely with professional staff, student employees, and volunteers to help promote and maintain a trauma-informed and inclusive environment for students experiencing food insecurity. Specific Duties Outreach & Promotion Create and distribute Leo Food Pantry promotional materials Plan, develop, and post social media content Promote pantry services at campus events Represent the Leo Food Pantry during outreach activities Assist with newsletter content, social media engagement, photography, success stories, and communication campaigns that highlight pantry impact and student resources. Student Engagement Build relationships with students and student organizations Gather feedback regarding Pantry services and student needs Assist with student awareness campaigns and support efforts to increase utilization of pantry resources. Donation Drive Leadership Plan, coordinate, and implement campus-based food, hygiene, and basic-needs donation drives, including recruiting participants, monitoring donations, and supporting collection and distribution efforts. Community Partnerships & Events Assist with outreach to campus departments, faculty, and community partners Support special events and awareness campaigns Customer Service & Access Greet pantry patrons and provide a welcoming, respectful, and confidential experience Assist students with food selection while maintaining dignity and choice Provide basic information and referrals to other campus student support or basic needs services, as appropriate Minimum Qualifications Current enrollment as an undergraduate student at the University of La Verne Availability to work a consistent schedule aligned with pantry hours and operational needs Ability to work independently and take initiative. Basic proficiency with technology and social media platforms Strong interpersonal and communication skills Ability to work effectively with diverse populations and maintain confidentiality Preferred Qualifications Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple tasks in a fast-paced environment Experience with student organizations, campus leadership, community service, or volunteer programs. Experience creating content for social media, marketing campaigns, newsletters, or events. Experience coordinating events, fundraisers, donation drives, or volunteer activities. Creative problem-solving skills and the ability to develop new ideas for promoting services and engaging the campus community. Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. Physical Demands Summary The physical demands include the ability to sit, stand, walk, bend, and lift up to 20 pounds occasionally. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? No If yes, list maximum weight and duration Describe work environment Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $17.40 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251597SE Special Instructions to Applicants Open Date 08/26/2026 Close Date 04/30/2027 Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15684 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15763": {
      "title": "Executive Director, Accounting and Treasury",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | Executive Director, Accounting and Treasury Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Executive Director, Accounting and Treasury Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The University of La Verne is unable to provide sponsorship for work visas at this time. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for visa sponsorship now or in the future. Job Vacancy Announcement Position Information Functional Title Executive Director, Accounting and Treasury Position Type Administrative/Professional Appointment Type Regular FTE % 100% Work Schedule (if atypical) University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary Reporting to the Associate Vice President of Finance, while working closely with the CFO . This position is responsible for the accounting function and reporting for the institution. In addition, this position also executes the functions of cash and financial forecasting, operating cash investments, liquidity, cash inflows and outflows, banking and financial institution relationships, and financial risk management related to the University’s financial activities Minimum Qualifications Strong understanding of all aspects of Non-profit Accounting through Financial Statement preparation. Knowledge of General Ledger software Experience in preparation of data for the Federal form 990 Ability to exercise a high degree of accurate and independent judgement, tact, and discretion. Strong analytical skills in evaluating situations and making decisions. Demonstrated commitment to providing excellent customer service and the ability to work with a broad constituency and develop effective working relations with University administrators, faculty, staff, students, and Trustees. Working knowledge of pooled endowments, including unitization, spending policies, asset allocations, funding transfers, and endowment financial reporting requirements. Supervisory experience required Strong organizational skills Strong time management skills Strong attention to detail Self-motivated Excellent verbal and written communication skill Preferred Qualifications Higher Education experience Knowledge of financial and treasury principles expected Advanced skill and knowledge of Microsoft Office software, especially Excel, and adept at using macos, V-lookup, creating charts and graph Benefits Summary Applicants, please note that actual compensation is determined by several factors that are unique to each candidate, including but not limited to job-related skills, depth of experience, certifications, relevant education or training, and specific work location, among others. The offered wage or salary is only one aspect of an employee’s total compensation Benefits include a comprehensive health and wellness plan, tuition remission program for employee, spouse, and dependent children, a generous contribution to the University’s 403B retirement plan, and a generous time off plan. Employment is contingent upon successful completion and clearance of a background check and employment verification. Location La Verne Main Campus Number of Vacancies 1 Physical Demands Summary 1. The physical demands include the ability to sit, stand, walk, bend, and lift up to 20 pounds occasionally. Clear verbal and written communication is essential, as the position involves frequent interaction with colleagues, clients, or external partners. 2. The noise level is generally low to moderate. The position may involves meeting deadlines or managing multiple priorities, which can require sustained focus and mental stamina. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? Yes If yes, list maximum weight and duration 20lbs Describe work environment This position is based in a standard office environment and primarily involves sedentary work. Employees are expected to spend extended periods of time working at a desk, using a computer, and engaging in routine office tasks such as emailing and phones. Duties Specific Duties Management of accounting function in the general ledger, and related sub ledgers. Monthly close process, including monthly checklist of reconciliations, standard journal entries, monthly reconciliations of bank accounts, quarterly review of capital assets, and GL balances in all funds. Percentage Of Time Specific Duties Monthly financial statement preparation and analysis for including but not limited to the Board of Trustees, Senior Management, Creditors, Rating Agencies. Percentage Of Time Specific Duties Preparation of annual audit workpapers Percentage Of Time Specific Duties Management of the annual audit and work with outside auditors Percentage Of Time Specific Duties Work with University tax accountants to prepare the University’s annual 990 and 590 tax reports Percentage Of Time Specific Duties Oversight of the following portfolios: endowment ($161M), operating cash ($100M), annuities and trusts ($2.8M), and student loan funds ($3M). Ensure that the University complies with the Investment Policy, Operating Cash Policy, and other financial polices and procedures as it pertains to investments. Develop strategies to maximize efficiencies, yields, safeguard assets and cost control. Percentage Of Time Specific Duties Overview and maintenance of all bank and investment accounts and the relationship with the various financial institutions, and investment managers. Administer Wells Fargo Bank CEO Portal, which requires set-up of all employee and student users, who require banking information, reports, or PCard access (approx. 150 users), program access, limits, and general University settings. Percentage Of Time Specific Duties Advise Management on the liquidity aspects of long and short-term financial planning. Monitor bank fees, and identify opportunities for savings. Percentage Of Time Specific Duties Manage and execute functions related to cash liquidity, bank, trustee, brokerage management, investment management. Work with University’s endowment management consultants in administering investments decisions approved by the Board Investment Committee. Develop financial models for investments, cash flow projections (sources and uses of cash), and other financial/treasury-related reports as needed for financial decisions and positions. Forecast cash flow positions, related borrowing needs, and available funds for investments. Ensure sufficient funds are available to meet ongoing operational and capital investment cash liquidity needs. Manage all banking access. Percentage Of Time Specific Duties Oversee the completion of various annual financial reports and surveys Percentage Of Time Specific Duties Assist in financial internal control development, implementation, and assessment. Percentage Of Time Specific Duties Work with and train operational units with Federal and State legislative compliance. Percentage Of Time Specific Duties Manage direct reports of all staff accountants Percentage Of Time Specific Duties Additional tasks as assigned by the Associate Vice President of Finance and HR, and the CFO . Percentage Of Time Specific Duties Attend, participate, and present in the Audit and Investment Committees of the Board of Trustees Percentage Of Time Salary Range Minimum: $124,347.83 Maximum: $137,437.43 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251207SA Special Instructions to Applicants The University of La Verne is unable to provide sponsorship for work visas at this time. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for visa sponsorship now or in the future. Open Date 10/21/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? HigherEdjobs.com AcademicCareers.com University of La Verne Website Referred by University of La Verne Employee Other Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
