    "https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15754": {
      "title": "Academic & Career Services Student Assistant (2 Positions)",
      "description": "University of La Verne Employment Opportunities | Academic &amp; Career Services Student Assistant (2 Positions) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Academic & Career Services Student Assistant (2 Positions) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. 1. Explain why you are interested in this position. 2. What days and times are you available to work? Please consider your class schedule, extracurricular activities, and other responsibilities. 3. Would you be interested/available to work during the summer months? Request to Recruit Information Position Recruitment Information Job Title Academic & Career Services Student Assistant (2 Positions) Student Position Type Federal Work Study Appointment Type Regular FTE Work Schedule Monday–Friday, 8 a.m.–5 p.m Approximately 10-20 hrs/week (Must commit to working 10 hrs/week MINIMUM ) Flexible with school schedule Department Manager Hiring Manager Lorie Ramiro-Rhodes Number of Vacancies 2 Position Summary Information for Announcement University Overview Embark on an exciting journey with the University of La Verne, where your career aspirations come to life in a vibrant and welcoming environment. Established in 1891, our diverse and inclusive community is more than just a university—it’s a home for passionate individuals like you. At the University of La Verne, we embody four core values that set us apart—Ethical Reasoning, Diversity and Inclusivity, Lifelong Learning, and Civic and Community Engagement. If you’re fueled by these principles and are eager to make a meaningful impact, your journey begins here. With a rich history spanning 132 years, the University of La Verne boasts a global Leo Family of 89,000+ accomplished alumni. As the #1 private university in California for social mobility according to U.S. News and World Report 2024, and recently recognized as the 33rd Best U.S. College by the Wall Street Journal 2024, we take pride in our commitment to excellence in education. Join us in shaping the future, where your passion meets purpose. Come be part of something extraordinary and apply today! Diversity Statement The University supports a diverse and inclusive environment where students recognize and benefit from the life experiences and viewpoints of other students, faculty, and staff. Diversity is an active and intentional practice that supports difference and multiplicity to expand knowledge, educate capable citizens, develop the whole person, and serve our local and global communities. Promoting and sustaining diversity is a commitment to educational quality and the creation of positive, respectful learning communities. Job Description Summary The student assistant in the Academic & Career Services Office will work closely with various student services departments. They will interact daily with students/parents/faculty and staff. The office is looking for someone to support staff in daily tasks and special projects and deliver excellent customer service. Specific Duties The student assistant will assist with clerical tasks such as: Answering phones Responding to emails Scheduling appointments Greeting and assisting walk-ins Managing student records General office work As well as: Always maintain other students’ confidentiality. Utilize the University’s student database (Banner, Handshake, and Big Interview) to provide information and make changes. Assist with management of student records Answer general questions about career, academic advising, and registration Assist with managing marketing via Canva Minimum Qualifications Student must be/have: Must be eligible for federal work-study Must be a current ULV student MINIMUM of 10 hours/week (20 hrs max. allowed per HR/CA law) Minimum 3.0 GPA Conscientious person who considers personal commitments and responsibilities seriously Ability to communicate effectively Strong organizational skills Attention to detail and accuracy Working knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, etc.) Willingness to learn new skills Preferred Qualifications Academic and Career Services would prefer applicants to be/have: First- or second-year TUG main campus students Office experience preferred, not required Customer service experience preferred, not required Knowledge of designing flyers in Canva Benefits Summary Employees are eligible for the following benefits: One hour of Paid Sick Leave for every 30 hours worked, with a maximum accrual of 24 hours of Paid Sick Leave per year and capped at 48 hours. University of La Verne Defined Contribution Retirement Plan – can contribute employee voluntary contributions, excluding wages derived from federal work study funds. In accordance with the Affordable Care Act ( ACA ), employees who work an average of 30 or more hours per week, will be eligible for medical coverage through the University of La Verne. Covered under the University of La Verne Workers Compensation Insurance. Location La Verne Main Campus If Other, please specify. Physical Demands Summary The physical demands include the ability to sit, stand, walk, bend, and lift up to 20 pounds occasionally. Do the essential functions of this job require lifting? No If yes, list maximum weight and duration Describe work environment Office Hiring Pay Rate Hourly Rate $16.90 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2024-251599SE Special Instructions to Applicants 1. Explain why you are interested in this position. 2. What days and times are you available to work? Please consider your class schedule, extracurricular activities, and other responsibilities. 3. Would you be interested/available to work during the summer months? Open Date 10/13/2026 Close Date 12/01/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Quick Link https://laverne.peopleadmin.com/postings/15753 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? HigherEdjobs.com AcademicCareers.com University of La Verne Website Referred by University of La Verne Employee Other * Explain why you are interested in this position. (Open Ended Question) * What days and times are you available to work? Please consider your class schedule, extracurricular activities, and other responsibilities. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents University of La Verne 1950 Third Street La Verne, CA 91750\r\n(909) 593-3511 © Copyright University of La Verne To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
